msm_drm sde_kms: free DSI/DP bridges only after the encoder detached them

Error paths of _sde_kms_setup_displays() (connector init failed, DSI ext bridge init
failed, DP connector init failed) freed the kzalloc'd bridge first and destroyed the
encoder afterwards. sde_encoder_destroy() -> drm_encoder_cleanup() walks
encoder->bridge_chain and calls drm_bridge_detach() on every bridge, so it touched freed
memory. On 6.12 that was list_del() + bridge->dev = NULL on the freed bridge; on 6.18
drm_bridge_detach() also does drm_bridge_put() (ack/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_bridge.c:487-504),
i.e. a kref_put() on freed memory, and if that memory was reused and read as 1 the core
calls __drm_bridge_free() -> kfree(bridge->container) on garbage (drm_bridge.c:208-215).
Order now: connector/encoder destroy (detach, refcount 2 -> 1), then the bridge kfree.

Error paths only (the A52s DSI path does not take them on a good boot); no change to the
success path. Applies on top of 0030 (0030 does not touch sde_kms.c).

--- a/drivers612/display/techpack/display-drivers/msm/sde/sde_kms.c
+++ b/drivers612/display/techpack/display-drivers/msm/sde/sde_kms.c
@@ -2093,8 +2093,12 @@
 			priv->connectors[priv->num_connectors++] = connector;
 		} else {
 			SDE_ERROR("dsi %d connector init failed\n", i);
-			dsi_display_drm_bridge_deinit(display);
+			/*
+			 * bsp618: detach the bridge (drm_encoder_cleanup()) before it
+			 * is freed; 6.18 drops the attach reference on detach.
+			 */
 			sde_encoder_destroy(encoder);
+			dsi_display_drm_bridge_deinit(display);
 			continue;
 		}
 
@@ -2102,9 +2106,10 @@
 					encoder, connector);
 		if (rc) {
 			SDE_ERROR("dsi %d ext bridge init failed\n", rc);
-			dsi_display_drm_bridge_deinit(display);
+			/* bsp618: free the bridge only after the encoder detached it */
 			sde_connector_destroy(connector);
 			sde_encoder_destroy(encoder);
+			dsi_display_drm_bridge_deinit(display);
 		}
 
 		dsc_count += info.dsc_count;
@@ -2178,8 +2183,9 @@
 			priv->connectors[priv->num_connectors++] = connector;
 		} else {
 			SDE_ERROR("dp %d connector init failed\n", i);
-			dp_drm_bridge_deinit(display);
+			/* bsp618: free the bridge only after the encoder detached it */
 			sde_encoder_destroy(encoder);
+			dp_drm_bridge_deinit(display);
 		}
 
 		/* update display cap to MST_MODE for DP MST encoders */
